    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 1st with a lineup anchored by **Christian Yelich**, whose 62.48 score makes him our clear offensive focal point. Despite the presence of a sub-4.00 xERA arm in Landen Roupp, **Christian Yelich** gains significant utility from his leadoff placement and a robust 13% dynamic platoon boost, providing high-ceiling potential in a lineup that otherwise faces some stiff competition. Supporting him, **Carson Benge** (51.46) and **Colt Keith** (51.06) provide necessary stability at the top of the order. **Colt Keith** specifically benefits from an aggressive profile against Griffin Jax; his leadoff role coupled with a slow SP delivery environment creates a prime opportunity to hunt for stolen bases\u2014a critical priority given the premium we place on the SB category.\n\nOur most difficult decision of the day involved **Junior Caminero**, who projects at a 50.29 despite facing the formidable Ty Madden (2.31 xERA). While the matchup is undeniably tough, his status as a cleanup hitter provides the RBI floor necessary to keep him ahead of the bench. **Chase Meidroth** (39.23) was the closest exclusion; he ultimately fell short because the optimizer favored the high-floor, high-volume order positions occupied by **Gary Sanchez** and **Luke Raley**. While **Luke Raley** is hitting in a challenging matchup against Austin Warren, his +7% platoon edge was the deciding factor in keeping him active over the bench options.\n\nManagement must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board. Should official lineups shuffle **Colt Keith** or **Carson Benge** out of the leadoff spot, those efficiency scores will drop immediately. We are intentionally holding **Dillon Dingler** and **Casey Schmitt** in reserve; while their underlying metrics remain intriguing, the current platoon disadvantages against today\u2019s starting pitchers make them sub-optimal for our immediate Roto pursuit. We are prioritizing daily efficiency over potential upside to manage our remaining game caps, ensuring the Zebras maintain a competitive pace without overextending.",
